          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The speaker asks for one hour in which the early blessing could be held. Already the mild west wind shakes down a shower of blossom — the loss begins within the very weather of flourishing. The shade just enjoyed holds autumn already: the leaves will turn pale and a storm will scatter them. The Klett witness carries all forty lines; Nims's page 169 stays uncollated.",
