          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The second stanza answers the wish to hold with an instruction: take your share. Whoever wants the fruit must reach promptly — ripening and germination overlap; what passes includes both loss and advent. Rain carries it outward: every downpour changes the beloved valley, and affection gives no exemption. Then the river: one does not swim in the same water twice; the swimmer enters what was watched from the bank.",
