          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The final imperative: beginning and end must draw together into one, faster than the objects flee. The opening wished an hour of held blessing; the ending asks a gathering across passage. The Muses' favour promises the imperishable, with thanks. Den Gehalt in deinem Busen — the content borne inwardly; die Form in deinem Geist — the formed expression carrying it onward. The relation is One in change (human-amplified: yes).",
